---
description: How to use the PaidSync MCP server for advertising work - check connections first, discover tools instead of guessing, read before writing, and get approval before any change to an ad account.
alwaysApply: false
---

When a request involves ad campaigns, ad spend, budgets, bids, keywords, audiences, creative, conversion tracking or marketing reports, use the PaidSync MCP server and its skills.

1. Call `paidsync_context` before other PaidSync tools. Work only with platforms and accounts the user has connected.
2. Find tools through `paidsync_context` (with `include_tools`) and read inputs with `paidsync_tool_detail`. Do not guess tool names or parameters.
3. Read and audit before proposing any change.
4. Draft every change to an ad account (budget, bid, status, targeting, new campaign or ad) and wait for the user's explicit yes before applying it.
5. Report only numbers returned by PaidSync in this session, with their account, date range and currency.
